.TH SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS3_SIXAXIS_DRIVER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS3_SIXAXIS_DRIVER \- A variable controlling whether the Sony driver (sixaxis.sys) for PS3 controllers (Sixaxis/DualShock 3) should be used.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS3_SIXAXIS_DRIVER \(dqSDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS3_SIXAXIS_DRIVER\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Sony driver (sixaxis\[char46]sys) is not used\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Sony driver (sixaxis\[char46]sys) is used\[char46]
.PP
The default value is 0\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before initializing joysticks and gamepads\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

